  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "How about + -ing: suggestions",
      "title_form": "How about + -ing: sugerencias",
      "title_target": "How about + -ing: suggestions",
      "description_md_form": "Para **sugerir** una actividad en inglés, usamos **How about + verbo con -ing**. Es una forma muy natural y amable de proponer planes.\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n> **How about + verbo(-ing) + ...?**\n\n**Ejemplos:**\n- `How about reading a book?` = ¿Qué te parece leer un libro?\n- `How about playing sports?` = ¿Qué te parece practicar deportes?\n\n**Uso:**\n- Se usa para **invitar** a alguien a hacer algo juntos.\n- Es una **pregunta**, pero no necesita respuesta con \"sí\" o \"no\".\n- La respuesta puede ser: `Good idea!` (¡Buena idea!) o `No problem.` (No hay problema).\n\n**Importante:** Después de **How about**, el verbo **siempre** termina en **-ing**. No se usa el verbo en infinitivo.",
      "description_md_target": "To **suggest** an activity in English, we use **How about + verb with -ing**. It is a very natural and friendly way to propose plans.\n\n**Structure:**\n\n> **How about + verb(-ing) + ...?**\n\n**Examples:**\n- `How about reading a book?` = What do you think about reading a book?\n- `How about playing sports?` = What do you think about playing sports?\n\n**Use:**\n- It is used to **invite** someone to do something together.\n- It is a **question**, but it does not need a \"yes\" or \"no\" answer.\n- The answer can be: `Good idea!` or `No problem.`\n\n**Important:** After **How about**, the verb **always** ends in **-ing**. We do not use the infinitive.",
      "grammar_structure": "How about + verb(-ing) + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "how_about_ing",
        "headers": [
          "Parte",
